entry.summary:
🧭 Day 10 — The Art of CSS Positioning Let’s break down what I learned 👇 🎯 Absolute Position — “The Floating Element Trick”
Then, I gave Box 1 the CSS rule: position: absolute;
And boom! Box 1 lifted off the layout like it just got gravity removed.
The space it left behind got filled by Box 2, and Box 3 moved up too — just like a Tetris game in motion.
Then I tried the same with Box 2 and Box 3.
💡 Note: 🧩 Relative Position — “Parent Matters!” outer (the parent) inner (the child) text (the grandchild) At first, I gave text the CSS: position: absolute; left: 50%;
It moved to the center — but not quite. It was taking 50% of the entire screen width, not its parent’s.
Then I gave its parent (inner) this: position: relative;
And boom 💥— the magic happened!
Now, left: 50% 💬 Reminde…
